+# Hi02 planet view from the NAP start save
+
+## Setup
+
+The Release client was built with the maintained overlay and run with the
+verified NAP-only application under Wayland, Mesa OpenGL 4.6, and Intel HD 4600
+at 1280x720. The active manifest contains 14 verified archives, including
+`planet-hdr-profile.nap` version 5. The test application has no loose `DATA`
+directory; the test save and package inputs are under `Data/NAP/`.
+
+The start save places the player at `(-27287, 0, -20000)` in Hi02 and stores
+`rotate = 0, 180, 0`, facing the planet at `(-27287, 0, -14869)`. Save loading
+previously discarded this rotation and substituted `Quaternion.Identity`;
+save writing also omitted it. Patch 2435 converts the saved Euler rotation on
+load and writes the character orientation back to the save.
+
+## Capture
+
+HDR, normal maps, and Surface PBR maps were enabled. Bloom, SSAO, and shadows
+were disabled. The screenshot option waited 120 loaded space frames after the
+spawn/cutscene transition. The capture shows the planet in the active Hi02
+scene, confirming that the start orientation reaches the camera-facing ship.
+
+![Hi02 planet view with HDR enabled](hi02-planet-hdr-on.png)
+
+The HDR-off retry loaded game data but did not reach `UI: Interface loaded`
+before its timeout, so it did not produce a comparable image. This capture is
+not a controlled HDR A/B or a complete material-quality acceptance. Further
+work must hold simulation and camera state fixed and compare the same planet
+frame with HDR on and off.
